==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm}} {{term|brawne|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|braon||slice of meat, fleshy part, buttock|lang=fro}}, of {{etyl|gem}} origin, from {{etyl|frk}} *{{term||brādon}}, accusative form of *{{term||brādo|roasted meat, ham}}, from {{proto|Germanic|brēdô|meat, roast|lang=en}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|bhre-|to burn, heat|lang=en}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|bureue-|to boil, bubble, burn|lang=en}}. Akin to {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|brato|brāto|tender meat|lang=goh}} ({{etyl|de|-}} {{term|Braten||roast|lang=de}}), {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|bræd|brǣd|flesh, meat|lang=ang}}, {{etyl|non|-}} {{term|bráð||raw meat|lang=non}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɔːn}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}
{{wikipedia|Head cheese|brawn}}

# Strong [[muscle]]s or [[lean]] [[flesh]], especially of the arm, leg or thumb.
# Physical [[strength]]; [[muscularity]].
# {{chiefly|British}} [[head cheese]]; a [[terrine]] made from the [[head]] of a [[pig]] or [[calf]]; originally [[boar]]'s meat.

